{# The mail that carries the address, and nothing else.

   No clause, no amount, no PDF: a mailbox is not where a contract should be
   readable, and a forwarded mail should carry a door rather than the room
   behind it. What it does say is what is being asked and by when, because a
   bare link asks somebody to click to find out. #}
<p>{{ 'accounting.email.contract_link.greeting'|trans({'{name}': customer.representativeFullName ?? customer.legalName}) }}</p>

<p>{{ 'accounting.email.contract_link.body'|trans({'{company}': siteName, '{reference}': contract.reference}) }}</p>

<p>
    <a href="{{ url }}">{{ 'accounting.email.contract_link.action'|trans }}</a>
</p>

<p>{{ 'accounting.email.contract_link.expiry'|trans({'{date}': expiresAt|date('d/m/Y')}) }}</p>

<p>{{ 'accounting.email.contract_link.warning'|trans }}</p>

<p>{{ 'accounting.email.contract_link.signature'|trans({'{company}': siteName}) }}</p>
